WEBVTT

00:17.810 --> 00:19.120
We've won, then?

00:19.120 --> 00:19.790
Yes, milady!

00:19.790 --> 00:22.050
We have a few dozen bandits in custody.

00:22.050 --> 00:24.570
Are my husband and Pas uninjured?

00:24.570 --> 00:26.380
His Lordship is safe.

00:26.630 --> 00:28.830
Lord Pas took a blow to the arm.

00:29.600 --> 00:30.670
A blow?

00:30.670 --> 00:32.390
Oh, what will I do?

00:32.390 --> 00:33.930
I'm sure it's just a scratch...

00:33.930 --> 00:35.180
Isn't it?

00:35.180 --> 00:36.400
Oh, of course!

00:36.400 --> 00:37.710
There's nothing to worry about.

00:40.300 --> 00:43.640
Surely they know Mother is 
sick with worry about them.

00:44.170 --> 00:47.610
Why haven't Father or Pas come home yet?

00:49.390 --> 00:51.480
The rightmost stack is for 
the main village here.

00:52.110 --> 00:55.030
Please take the remainder 
back to your own villages.

00:55.030 --> 00:56.230
Milord!

01:02.290 --> 01:07.290
<i>This is the tale of a genius patissier 
who died before his time,</i>

01:07.290 --> 01:11.530
<i>and was reincarnated as the son 
of a poor noble in another world</i>

01:11.530 --> 01:14.680
<i>to pursue a world full 
of desserts and smiles.</i>

01:15.550 --> 01:20.290
<i>It's a tale that is at once cold 
and unsparing, and syrupy sweet.</i>

01:21.690 --> 01:28.100
<i>His dream is to create this 
world's very own land of sweets!</i>

01:36.030 --> 01:38.610
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

03:00.990 --> 03:07.060
<b>Apple Pie and Smiles</b>

03:03.450 --> 03:06.540
Keep them all tied up separately!

03:06.540 --> 03:07.460
My lord!

03:11.620 --> 03:15.660
Is the plan still to ship them 
off to the County of Retes?

03:15.660 --> 03:17.290
That seems the most sensible way.

03:17.660 --> 03:21.580
They can claim they dealt with the bandits 
rather than simply driving them out.

03:21.580 --> 03:24.370
That will allow the Count to save face.

03:24.790 --> 03:27.930
And what sort of gratitude 
can we expect in return?

03:27.930 --> 03:30.290
We'll have to talk that out.

03:30.720 --> 03:33.800
We'll at least need compensation 
for our campaign expenses,

03:33.800 --> 03:38.170
and the losses suffered from temporarily 
sealing the other two villages.

03:39.040 --> 03:40.860
Next! Glacage!

03:41.750 --> 03:42.750
My lord!

03:42.750 --> 03:45.410
For tremendous contributions 
to the front-line defense,

03:45.410 --> 03:47.910
I award you one spear and one silver coin!

03:48.720 --> 03:50.370
Thank you, my lord!

03:50.730 --> 03:53.330
Next! Marcarullo, Luminito!

03:53.330 --> 03:55.290
Coming! Coming!

03:56.040 --> 03:58.390
Why'd he call us both together?

03:58.390 --> 03:59.730
That's what I wanna know!

03:59.730 --> 04:03.760
You both served well as Pas's assistants.

04:04.020 --> 04:06.970
I award you each a sword and a bag of barley!

04:07.430 --> 04:08.520
Score!

04:09.840 --> 04:11.430
Th-Thanks!

04:14.750 --> 04:17.610
Kinda makes you blush, right, Lumi?

04:17.610 --> 04:19.630
Yeah.

04:19.630 --> 04:22.250
And boy, this is heavy...

04:22.250 --> 04:23.710
I'll help!

04:23.710 --> 04:25.700
Pas! Thanks so much!

04:26.330 --> 04:28.200
You both did so great!

04:29.400 --> 04:31.270
Maybe not as good as you, Pas...

04:31.270 --> 04:33.280
But we kinda held our own, right?

04:33.280 --> 04:36.290
I totally threw more stones than you, though!

04:37.130 --> 04:40.590
I'm the one who hit that bandit 
in the head at the end!

04:38.180 --> 04:41.180
<i>I'm so glad that no one died,</i>

04:41.180 --> 04:44.550
The next suzerain lord will 
be just fine with us around!

04:41.670 --> 04:43.690
<i>and we can get right back to life as it was.</i>

04:44.550 --> 04:46.890
You can put your full trust in us.

04:46.890 --> 04:48.380
I'm relying on you both.

04:49.650 --> 04:51.210
Mom, look!

04:51.210 --> 04:53.980
His Lordship granted me 
a sword for my service!

04:54.340 --> 04:55.940
Some barley, too!

04:55.940 --> 04:57.640
You're awesome, Big Brother!

04:57.640 --> 04:58.650
Awthome!

04:58.920 --> 05:03.860
You made it home safely. 
That's all I care about.

05:04.970 --> 05:09.530
My fool of a son didn't cause 
you any trouble, did he, milord?

05:10.010 --> 05:13.000
Marc and Lumi both did great!

05:13.810 --> 05:18.300
I think they'll both be indispensable 
to Morteln's future!

05:19.290 --> 05:22.670
Great work, Lumi! That's my grandkid!

05:22.670 --> 05:24.810
Hey, that hurts!

05:25.690 --> 05:29.810
To think you'd be aiding our lord 
and his son at such a young age!

05:28.190 --> 05:31.270
Grandpa, you're breaking my back!

05:31.270 --> 05:33.130
We brought the wine, sir!

05:33.130 --> 05:34.880
Sure, come on in!

05:34.880 --> 05:36.690
It's time to celebrate our victory!

05:37.370 --> 05:39.880
Eh? Your father's not back yet?

05:39.880 --> 05:44.650
Yeah, he said he still had 
some business with Marc's dad.

05:44.650 --> 05:46.800
It's a shame we missed him!

05:46.800 --> 05:49.870
But hey, the young lord is here!

05:49.870 --> 05:51.490
Great timing!

05:51.490 --> 05:53.130
Come celebrate with us!

05:53.130 --> 05:54.930
Oh, I'd love to!

05:54.930 --> 05:56.070
Can we drink?!

05:56.070 --> 05:59.390
Don't be stupid! You and 
the young lord get milk!

05:59.390 --> 06:00.230
Shucks.

06:01.590 --> 06:04.050
Cheers!

06:05.650 --> 06:07.880
I can't believe Lumi and Marc got rewards!

06:07.880 --> 06:12.690
Seriously! I thought those little 
rapscallions were nothing but trouble!

06:12.690 --> 06:15.990
Now I can walk down the road 
with my head held high!

06:15.990 --> 06:19.270
Ah, but the children's ambush the 
young lord led was truly magnificent!

06:19.270 --> 06:22.890
Long live our next suzerain lord!

06:20.810 --> 06:23.820
<i>Now, at last, I can focus on making sweets!</i>

06:23.820 --> 06:26.770
<i>Yes! I'm gonna make me a bonka pie!</i>

06:26.770 --> 06:28.490
<i>To make it, I need...</i>

06:28.990 --> 06:29.950
<i>Butter,</i>

06:30.510 --> 06:31.410
<i>flour,</i>

06:31.970 --> 06:32.870
<i>eggs...</i>

06:33.430 --> 06:37.500
<i>Ah, but I'll still need 
something like cinnamon...</i>

06:38.360 --> 06:42.040
Sheesh! I'm so used to everyone 
always yelling at us,

06:42.040 --> 06:44.290
it feels sorta weird when 
they say nice things, y'know?

06:44.550 --> 06:47.120
Always yelling at <i>you</i>, you mean.

06:47.120 --> 06:49.510
Aw, c'mon! You get yelled at, too!

06:50.420 --> 06:53.470
Say, what do you think 
they did with the bandits?

06:53.720 --> 06:56.430
They put 'em in the shed 
in the main village, right?

06:56.670 --> 06:58.510
Let's go check 'em out!

06:58.910 --> 07:01.340
As future retainers to the lord of this land,

07:01.340 --> 07:04.270
it's our duty to monitor the prisoners!

07:04.620 --> 07:05.730
Right!

07:09.910 --> 07:12.570
It's not safe for children to be here!

07:12.570 --> 07:14.160
C'mon, it'll just be a second!

07:14.430 --> 07:17.070
I said no! Go home!

07:17.070 --> 07:19.010
C'mon, you stingy jerk!

07:19.740 --> 07:22.990
Treating us like kids... those big jerks!

07:29.530 --> 07:31.070
What's gotten into you?!

07:32.220 --> 07:33.970
Just watch this!

07:38.640 --> 07:39.790
Wh-What was that?

07:39.790 --> 07:40.930
It came from back there!

07:54.380 --> 07:56.200
H-H-Hey...

07:57.050 --> 07:58.660
Not so tough, are they?

07:58.660 --> 07:59.900
Hey, kid.

08:00.530 --> 08:02.160
That sword on your hip.

08:02.760 --> 08:04.010
Where'd you get it?

08:04.010 --> 08:06.410
I-It was a reward!

08:06.410 --> 08:09.030
See, that used to be my sword.

08:10.000 --> 08:13.300
Once they turn me in, I'm dead for sure.

08:14.070 --> 08:18.850
Before I die, I'd like to teach 
you how to <i>really</i> use my sword...

08:19.110 --> 08:20.780
How to <i>really</i> use it?

08:20.780 --> 08:22.060
Well, yeah.

08:22.060 --> 08:25.650
If you use it right, it'll let you use magic!

08:25.650 --> 08:26.710
Magic?!

08:27.350 --> 08:28.820
<i>Like Pas?</i>

08:28.820 --> 08:32.780
Draw the sword and hold it up in both hands.

08:32.780 --> 08:37.020
C'mon, Marc. Don't listen to that jerk!

08:37.540 --> 08:38.920
L-Like this?

08:38.920 --> 08:40.160
Marc!

08:40.160 --> 08:43.210
Yeah, that's right. You're a natural.

08:43.210 --> 08:45.270
R-Really?

08:45.270 --> 08:47.120
Now, say the magic words.

08:47.120 --> 08:48.170
Magic words?

08:48.600 --> 08:52.630
It's pretty dangerous, so I don't 
wanna let your friend there hear.

08:52.630 --> 08:54.130
Come in close.

08:58.340 --> 09:00.010
What're the magic words?

09:00.010 --> 09:01.840
Listen up...

09:03.310 --> 09:04.430
Marc!

09:16.260 --> 09:17.730
Lumi!

09:24.470 --> 09:25.660
What happened?!

09:27.410 --> 09:28.830
Stay back!

09:29.180 --> 09:30.790
Emergency!

09:31.610 --> 09:33.640
One of the bandits hurt Lumi!

09:33.640 --> 09:34.960
What?!

09:34.960 --> 09:36.470
One of the bandits?

09:39.680 --> 09:40.810
Oh, no!

09:43.170 --> 09:45.770
Outta the way, or the kid loses his head!

09:45.770 --> 09:47.860
Someone tell His Lordship!

09:47.860 --> 09:49.980
Surround him! Don't let him escape!

09:50.340 --> 09:52.690
Chief, save us too!

09:52.920 --> 09:54.140
Screw you!

09:54.140 --> 09:56.510
If you wanna be saved, do it yourselves!

09:59.920 --> 10:01.570
Lumi! You okay?

10:04.740 --> 10:06.170
What are you doing?

10:08.670 --> 10:10.380
Lumi needs treatment at once.

10:10.380 --> 10:11.840
Lumi! Lumi!

10:15.180 --> 10:16.360
Stop the bleeding.

10:16.730 --> 10:19.050
It doesn't matter if it leaves a scar!

10:19.050 --> 10:20.260
R-Right!

10:21.600 --> 10:22.410
Where's the bandit?

10:22.410 --> 10:24.280
He stole a horse and fled!

10:24.280 --> 10:25.120
In which direction?

10:25.120 --> 10:26.540
To the east!

10:26.540 --> 10:27.510
<i>The east...</i>

10:28.170 --> 10:29.440
Look after Lumi!

10:32.790 --> 10:36.940
<i>The traps set in the east mountains to 
deter the bandits should still be in place.</i>

10:38.290 --> 10:41.190
<i>If I can avoid a fatal blow, 
I can use my replication</i>

10:41.190 --> 10:44.100
<i>to copy any wound I receive back onto him.</i>

10:44.100 --> 10:46.650
<i>If worse comes to worst, I can force a draw.</i>

10:48.510 --> 10:49.510
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

10:50.840 --> 10:53.500
<i>If I can replicate anything I see...</i>

10:54.500 --> 10:55.420
<i>Is it possible...</i>

10:56.420 --> 10:59.330
And then Pas went in pursuit on his own?!

10:59.330 --> 11:01.850
You idiot! Why didn't you stop him?!

11:02.260 --> 11:04.180
I-It happened so quickly...

11:05.050 --> 11:06.690
Feuille, follow me.

11:06.690 --> 11:07.810
I'll go.

11:08.200 --> 11:10.210
If he's got allies out there,

11:10.210 --> 11:12.800
they could meet up and turn 
the tables on their pursuers.

11:13.530 --> 11:16.820
You should stay here with 
Glacage and get ready.

11:18.010 --> 11:19.280
Feuille?

11:19.610 --> 11:23.220
If word of the escape gets out, it will 
be a blow to the villagers' morale.

11:23.220 --> 11:29.440
At times like this, your job is to make 
a show of strength and reassure them.

11:34.890 --> 11:36.350
Summon Cointreau.

11:36.350 --> 11:37.130
Sir!

11:38.400 --> 11:40.100
Let me go!

11:40.100 --> 11:42.550
Lemme go already!

11:42.550 --> 11:44.510
Annoying little brat!

11:44.510 --> 11:45.470
Just shut u—

11:49.270 --> 11:51.640
D-Damn it!

11:52.310 --> 11:53.480
Ouch...

11:55.990 --> 11:57.150
Pas!

12:01.260 --> 12:02.780
You again!

12:03.270 --> 12:06.990
Are you the one who set this 
stupid little trap, too?

12:06.990 --> 12:10.700
You've got some wiles for a little brat...

12:11.430 --> 12:13.190
Marc, stay back!

12:14.050 --> 12:16.630
You want a real duel, eh?

12:18.180 --> 12:21.590
<i>Hold it so tight, I could tear 
off your hands before you'd let go!</i>

12:22.110 --> 12:24.000
Bring it on, kid.

12:28.460 --> 12:31.480
Nice charge for a brat!

12:35.850 --> 12:38.750
<i>He might think he can replicate 
a wound onto me with his magic...</i>

12:38.750 --> 12:40.020
<i>I won't let him!</i>

12:40.020 --> 12:42.280
<i>I'll finish him off in a single stroke!</i>

12:46.480 --> 12:47.530
What's the matter, brat?

12:47.530 --> 12:49.870
Pas, run! I'm not worth it!

12:49.870 --> 12:53.080
No! I'll never abandon you, Marc!

12:55.050 --> 12:57.850
You're my lieutenant, remember?

12:58.320 --> 12:59.500
Pas...

12:59.500 --> 13:02.170
What a beautiful show of friendship!

13:05.080 --> 13:07.390
So long, brat!

13:08.850 --> 13:11.280
Pas!

13:19.770 --> 13:21.300
I can't find him!

13:21.300 --> 13:22.890
Where'd he get off to?

13:23.260 --> 13:25.960
Kid!

13:27.710 --> 13:30.450
The horse came from this direction!

13:31.070 --> 13:32.480
Marc!

13:32.480 --> 13:34.010
Lord Pas!

13:36.250 --> 13:37.350
Is this...

13:38.530 --> 13:39.540
The kid's sword...

13:48.720 --> 13:51.050
How am I going to tell them?

13:53.900 --> 13:56.640
Oh! Welcome back, Feuille!

14:01.060 --> 14:03.530
Kid?!

14:03.530 --> 14:06.490
He returned here with Marc not long ago.

14:06.890 --> 14:09.080
I got Marc home.

14:09.410 --> 14:12.310
Agnes took Pas in her arms 
and refused to let go,

14:13.020 --> 14:14.970
and eventually fell asleep just like that.

14:15.410 --> 14:17.350
So I just missed them on the way back?!

14:17.350 --> 14:18.290
I'm sorry.

14:18.630 --> 14:20.030
It's not possible!

14:20.030 --> 14:23.370
We followed right after him!
 How'd he get past us?!

14:23.980 --> 14:26.090
Pas, explain yourself.

14:26.370 --> 14:29.450
Well... about that, you see...

14:29.450 --> 14:31.510
It's an extremely complicated 
set of circumstances

14:31.510 --> 14:34.270
requiring a highly detailed explanation...

14:34.270 --> 14:36.100
So if it could wait, 
perhaps, for another day...

14:36.350 --> 14:37.310
Pas!

14:38.290 --> 14:42.770
I replicated Father's magic onto 
myself earlier and used that.

14:42.770 --> 14:44.570
My teleportation?

14:44.570 --> 14:46.230
You replicated it onto yourself?

14:46.470 --> 14:49.670
My magic lets me replicate 
a copy of anything onto anything else,

14:49.670 --> 14:54.390
as long as it's countable and I've 
seen or interfaced with the original.

14:55.700 --> 14:58.750
That includes other people's magic spells.

15:00.250 --> 15:01.770
And so...

15:04.450 --> 15:06.740
I had a feeling that's what it was.

15:06.740 --> 15:09.550
Pas, a word of warning for you.

15:09.550 --> 15:11.490
Y-Yes?

15:11.910 --> 15:19.480
<b>Lecture Lecture Lecture</b>

15:12.080 --> 15:16.950
You are hereby forbidden from telling anyone 
you can use other people's magic spells,

15:16.950 --> 15:19.480
or using those spells in front of others!

15:19.700 --> 15:22.120
Use of magic on the battlefield 
is extremely dangerous!

15:22.120 --> 15:26.690
Using it the wrong way could 
kill you very quickly!

15:26.690 --> 15:28.940
You may have replicated my 
teleportation onto yourself,

15:28.940 --> 15:33.320
but you could still teleport inside 
of a rock or deep into the ground!

15:33.700 --> 15:35.660
<i>I knew this would happen!</i>

15:38.860 --> 15:44.080
If it got out that he could 
replicate any other form of magic,

15:44.510 --> 15:48.410
others might come after 
him as a human weapon.

15:48.410 --> 15:52.200
I wish we hadn't let that 
bandit leader get away.

15:52.200 --> 15:57.600
We'll just have to pray he's disposed 
of before he reveals the secret.

16:03.810 --> 16:06.520
It sounds like Lumi's going to pull through.

16:07.730 --> 16:09.550
I was about to pay her a visit.

16:09.890 --> 16:11.370
Want to come along?

16:13.520 --> 16:15.320
How am I supposed to face her?

16:16.720 --> 16:19.290
It's my fault. My fault...

16:19.910 --> 16:24.270
If I'd listened to Lumi and 
just ignored that bandit,

16:24.270 --> 16:25.690
she never would've been hurt.

16:26.170 --> 16:29.500
Moping around here won't 
make things any better.

16:30.060 --> 16:31.540
Say you're sorry <i>to her</i>.

16:39.770 --> 16:42.100
Hey! To what do I owe 
these two fine visitors?

16:42.380 --> 16:44.030
How are you healing up?

16:44.030 --> 16:46.560
Dad says I'm all better now...

16:46.910 --> 16:49.810
But when I try to go out 
to play, he yells at me!

16:50.990 --> 16:52.870
I'm glad you seem well.

16:52.870 --> 16:55.030
I'm going to borrow your kitchen.

16:56.420 --> 16:58.490
Marc, what's got you so down?

17:01.350 --> 17:06.490
<i>What I want to do now isn't 
fighting or dealing with bandits.</i>

17:08.060 --> 17:10.400
<i>It's bringing smiles to faces!</i>

18:21.380 --> 18:22.310
Lumi...

18:22.650 --> 18:23.370
I'm sorry!

18:24.050 --> 18:25.690
H-Hey, where'd that come from?!

18:25.690 --> 18:26.830
You're freaking me out!

18:27.080 --> 18:30.040
But... it's my fault you got injured!

18:30.360 --> 18:31.920
It's fine.

18:31.920 --> 18:34.000
The bandit's the one who did it.

18:34.000 --> 18:36.260
But only 'cause I was a total idiot!

18:36.260 --> 18:38.410
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

18:38.410 --> 18:40.530
I told you, it's fine!

18:50.190 --> 18:52.930
What smells so good?

18:53.460 --> 18:55.500
Sounds you you got out a proper apology.

18:56.610 --> 18:59.070
Wh-What's that? It looks delicious!

18:59.370 --> 19:00.520
It's apple--

19:00.520 --> 19:02.610
I mean, bonka pie!

19:02.610 --> 19:03.780
Bonka pie?!

19:03.780 --> 19:07.850
My way of helping Lumi feel 
better, and cheering up Marc.

19:07.850 --> 19:09.750
Go on, try it!

19:10.010 --> 19:12.460
Awesome! That one's mine!

19:12.460 --> 19:15.210
Hey, I was gonna take that one!

19:16.400 --> 19:18.280
Early bird gets the worm!

19:21.330 --> 19:23.450
It's good!

19:23.450 --> 19:25.790
It's good! It's so darn good!

19:25.790 --> 19:28.090
My wound doesn't even hurt anymore!

19:28.090 --> 19:29.710
Glad to hear it!

19:29.710 --> 19:31.360
Try these, too!

19:31.760 --> 19:33.750
Bonkas in honey!

19:37.050 --> 19:40.280
S-So sour!

19:40.550 --> 19:41.470
Right?

19:41.470 --> 19:43.930
These are really the same fruit?!

19:43.930 --> 19:44.890
Yes!

19:44.890 --> 19:50.210
Every bonka tastes different. 
Some are sweeter, some are tart.

19:50.520 --> 19:52.470
When an ingredient is that idiosyncratic,

19:52.470 --> 19:56.590
you need real skill to prepare it in 
a way that harmonizes the flavors.

19:57.060 --> 19:59.300
I think it's the same with people.

19:59.580 --> 20:02.970
Marc, you have your own 
aspects that make you unique,

20:02.970 --> 20:05.220
and I'm going to make those aspects shine!

20:05.530 --> 20:06.870
Pas...

20:06.870 --> 20:10.270
I think this experience has 
deepened your flavor profile.

20:10.650 --> 20:13.480
I want you to take what you've learned 
from this and work hard to improve.

20:14.060 --> 20:17.280
If you're gonna be my lieutenant, that is!

20:19.140 --> 20:20.900
I am! I totally am!

20:23.680 --> 20:26.690
Marc...

20:26.690 --> 20:28.250
Hey, Dad! Welcome back!

20:28.250 --> 20:30.330
S-Sir...

20:30.330 --> 20:35.790
You've wounded my precious 
daughter, have you?!

20:36.180 --> 20:38.590
G-Glacage, calm down!

20:40.320 --> 20:45.010
Guess you'll have to make up for 
it by marrying my Lumi some day!

20:46.980 --> 20:50.680
This little tomboy of mine ain't 
gonna land a man on her own!

20:50.680 --> 20:52.780
M-Marry?!

20:51.750 --> 20:52.850
Sound good to you, Lumi?

20:52.850 --> 20:54.270
Of course it doe—

20:54.270 --> 20:55.180
Sounds fine to me.

20:59.050 --> 21:00.310
Well, that's that!

21:02.520 --> 21:04.070
Just four slices left, huh?

21:04.410 --> 21:05.330
Here.

21:05.330 --> 21:07.030
What's this, now?

21:07.030 --> 21:09.580
Bonka pie. Pas made it.

21:09.580 --> 21:11.190
Help yourself, Glacage.

21:11.190 --> 21:12.420
As you wish.

21:12.420 --> 21:14.040
Hey, what about mine?!

21:14.500 --> 21:17.750
A husband's assets belong to his wife, right?

21:19.060 --> 21:22.380
Which means I'm taking 
all the rest of the pie!

21:23.390 --> 21:25.340
She's cracking the whip already, eh?

21:25.340 --> 21:26.720
Better keep your wits about you!

21:28.690 --> 21:30.220
<i>So good!</i>

21:32.010 --> 21:35.230
<i>Sweets really do bring smiles to faces.</i>

21:35.540 --> 21:37.830
<i>But I'm just getting started!</i>

21:37.830 --> 21:39.380
That's great!

21:39.380 --> 21:40.670
<i>I'm gonna do it!</i>

21:40.670 --> 21:44.190
<i>I'm gonna make everyone 
happy in a land of sweets!</i>

23:17.420 --> 23:20.710
The bandits were dispatched 
in the Fief of Morteln?

23:20.710 --> 23:21.810
Yes.

23:21.810 --> 23:27.170
They rounded up every single one of 
the stragglers from our territory.

23:30.080 --> 23:33.220
Dealing with this could be quite troublesome.

23:37.000 --> 23:38.860
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>...

23:39.120 --> 23:45.020
<b>A Spicy Negotiation and Sweet Baked Treats</b>

23:39.210 --> 23:43.570
"A Spicy Negotiation and Sweet Baked Treats."

23:45.020 --> 23:50.250
<b>Illustration:</b>
